sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch07-11> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Detailed visual similarities in organisms imply intrinsic randomness" ;
    dct:description "Detailed visual similarities between members of the same species, and between the two symmetric sides of a system, in features that look complex and random cannot be attributed to environmental or initial-condition randomness and must come from intrinsic randomness generation." ;
    delphi:context "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 7, “Mechanisms in Programs and Nature”; section “The Intrinsic Generation of Randomness” (from p. 315), p. 326. Scope: complex-looking patterns in physical, biological and other systems, especially bilaterally symmetric ones" ;
    dct:type "model-of-nature" .
}

